1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,600
Your people and agents
see different truths.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,520
The truth is scattered across
the systems where work happens.

3
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:09,460
People rebuild it by hand.

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,170
Agents start without it.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,960
Navis turns those signals
into one shared understanding.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:18,550
Inside a company,
the Navis App is for people.

7
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:22,240
It shows what changed —
and why it matters.

8
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:26,400
Every fact has its source,
its time, and how fresh it is.

9
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:29,050
A person decides.

10
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,680
Then the company acts.

11
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,120
The same company's agents
use Navis Developer.

12
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:41,620
Connect once — through
MCP, API, SDK or CLI.

13
00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:43,150
The agent asks —

14
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:47,480
and gets the company's context,
with sources and freshness.

15
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:49,750
Navis isn't the model.

16
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,800
It supplies the company's truth.

17
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,380
The agent does the work,
and the run is on record.

18
00:00:56,830 --> 00:00:57,880
Same facts.

19
00:00:58,210 --> 00:00:59,260
Same sources.

20
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,710
Same freshness.

21
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,360
One understanding.

22
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:03,780
Two ways in.

23
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:05,270
NavisLabs.

24
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,420
The shared understanding
for your organization.

